{"id": 35, "ts": 1780595811.7379668, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m leaning toward Candidate\u202fC now. While we\u2019ve all highlighted Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability, stress handling and technical skills, we still have no concrete evidence of his decision quality in safety\u2011critical moments (James confirmed there are no such examples). In contrast, Sarah pointed out that Candidate\u202fC \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d giving us a clear indicator of strong decision\u2011making under time pressure\u2014exactly what long\u2011haul flights demand. Moreover, Sarah also noted that C creates a positive crew atmosphere and puts concern for others above everything, which suggests good crew cooperation despite his difficulty communicating ideas and being perceived as egocentric. The decision\u2011quality strength, combined with his excellent attention skills and reliability, outweighs the communication quirks, especially given B\u2019s pretentious tone and occasional uncooperative behavior. Until we hear any evidence that C cannot handle stress, I believe he is the better overall fit."}
